WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.370
So we do have primary elections today.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:09.570
Three of the four scheduled primaries are
happening today despite what is going on with

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:15.610
Corona virus, Arizona, Florida, Illinois and
Ohio were scheduled to vote.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:20.350
Now Ohio Governor Mike DeWine, who's a Republican,
announced.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:21.440
Polls are closed.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:26.780
The Ohio primary is postponed and tentatively
for June.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:32.890
Although who on earth knows at this point
what our world will look like in three months,

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:37.329
it's hard to imagine what it will even look
like in 10 days if the current infection numbers

00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:38.780
continue.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:40.390
This is do or die for Bernie.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:45.810
I mean, if Joe Biden picks up more than an
additional hundred delegate lead on Bernie

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:49.899
tonight, you know, Bernie has a hypothetical
path right now, although it's unlikely it's

00:00:49.899 --> 00:00:51.809
already a longshot.

00:00:51.809 --> 00:00:56.850
If Bernie falls another hundred delegates
behind tonight, it's essentially done.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.520
So we'll look at national polling, we'll look
at delegate counts, we'll look at state polls

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:06.350
and figure out sort of what to expect tonight
in terms of the delegate count going in.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:11.180
It's a hundred and fifty one delegate lead
for Joseph R. Biden, junior.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.690
Ninety four to seven.

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:21.000
We believed that tonight we were going to
have a total of 577 delegates available.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.060
That's Arizona, Florida, Illinois and Ohio.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:28.990
Florida, of course, the big prize with 219
delegates.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:32.030
Ohio postponing their primary.

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:39.060
So the 136 delegates out of Ohio will be saved
for another day, so to speak.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:45.350
Now, in terms of the polling, as you know,
nationally, Bernie Sanders has hit a ceiling

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:48.409
of about 36 percent.

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:53.890
And nationally, Joe Biden is leading the last
dozen or so polls, most recently by as much

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:55.870
as 29.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:02:03.150
Bernie did manage to get 38 percent in one
in the latest Economist YouGov poll.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:07.170
But the numbers looking very, very solid for
the former vise president.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:12.690
Looking state by state at polling in the states
that were scheduled to vote today in Arizona,

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:15.370
Joe Biden averaging plus 18.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:18.740
In Florida, Joe Biden averaging plus thirty
nine.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:22.160
Illinois has Biden at plus twenty nine and
a half.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:27.160
And Ohio, which again, has postponed their
primary as of now until sometime in June.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:28.290
Who knows?

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.300
Biden was up 22 and a half.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.590
I'm not even going to do delegate estimates
for what it will look like at the end of the

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:35.590
night.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:39.430
I mean, I think we all know that with these
margins, if the margins hold.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:46.320
It's a very bad night for Bernie Sanders and
a huge debate over whether anybody should

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.280
be voting at all because of what, you know,
we have on the one hand and we'll get to it.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.310
Donald Trump yesterday saying officially for
the country, you shouldn't have more than

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:56.010
10 people together.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:59.930
You kids shouldn't be at schools, restaurants
and bars should close.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:04.660
And we may have to continue some version of
this up until July or August.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:09.570
And then meanwhile, Florida, Illinois and
Arizona have huge crowds of people, presumably

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:11.060
assuming people are showing up to vote.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:15.630
And we will we will find out in just a few
hours congregating and doing all of the things

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.210
Donald Trump says they are not supposed to
do.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:24.290
There was the idea that maybe the debate between
Bernie Sanders and Joe Biden on Sunday night

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.409
would change the numbers.

00:03:26.409 --> 00:03:27.409
It didn't.

00:03:27.409 --> 00:03:32.500
We got we now have post debate polls and the
numbers are essentially unchanged.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:38.830
It was scheduled to be a debate with an audience
in Arizona because of the virus.

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:44.879
The change was made to do it in a studio with
just the candidates and three moderators with

00:03:44.879 --> 00:03:48.319
CNN in Washington, D.C..

00:03:48.319 --> 00:03:54.519
And again, the you know, I think that there
were a lot of people e-mailing me, expecting

00:03:54.519 --> 00:04:00.920
Biden to implode, unable to speak because
of his supposed dementia, which has been a

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:05.590
story being pushed not only by people on the
right, but also some people on the left.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:11.530
And the problem is the expectation was that
Biden would so miserably implode.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:16.459
Biden just had to be coherent for the debate
and he was unlikely to really be damaged.

00:04:16.459 --> 00:04:17.459
And that's what happened.

00:04:17.459 --> 00:04:23.020
You know, there were some disagreements, disagreements
about how to deal with the virus there.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:28.080
I think Bernie's strongest moment during the
two person debate on Sunday night was when

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.270
they started talking about Social Security.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:33.600
But again, it didn't seem like it was going
to make a difference.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.740
I tweeted that I didn't think it was going
to make a difference.

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:41.259
We now have debate, but post-debate polling
and it has not made a difference so far.

00:04:41.259 --> 00:04:47.949
So we are going to know very soon what at
least in Arizona, Illinois and Florida, Democratic

00:04:47.949 --> 00:04:50.520
voters who choose to go have decided.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:56.650
The other idea that's been floated has been
because old folks are more at risk if they

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:58.880
get the virus.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:04:59.880
Old folks.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:04.550
May disproportionately stay home, which will
hurt Biden and help Bernie.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.379
That was floated last week as well.

00:05:06.379 --> 00:05:11.999
Now, of course, in a week a lot has changed
when it comes to the virus and to people being

00:05:11.999 --> 00:05:13.249
told to stay home.

00:05:13.249 --> 00:05:15.089
We'll know within hours.

00:05:15.089 --> 00:05:20.400
At this point, I don't know that it makes
much sense to speculate beyond these ideas.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:25.159
We will have a results live stream starting
tonight at 8:00 p.m. Eastern Time on Twitch,

00:05:25.159 --> 00:05:26.699
YouTube and Facebook live.

00:05:26.699 --> 00:05:28.000
I hope you'll join me.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:33.729
We will take in the results together in what
are very, very strange times at this point.

00:05:33.729 --> 00:05:39.990
Quite frankly, I for me, it's been every morning
I wake up sometimes a few minutes before my

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:42.349
alarm, sometimes with my alarm.

00:05:42.349 --> 00:05:45.999
And there's I would call it a five second
period.

00:05:45.999 --> 00:05:51.590
It's probably more a fraction of a second
where I forget what's going on with current

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:52.590
coronavirus.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.979
It feels normal for just like a fraction of
a second.

00:05:54.979 --> 00:05:58.749
And then I remember that that's not the case.

00:05:58.749 --> 00:06:03.719
And we've shifted around our entire production
to to adjust to trying to stay away from people

00:06:03.719 --> 00:06:04.970
and crowds.

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:07.669
I am, you know, mostly just home.

00:06:07.669 --> 00:06:08.970
This could go on for months.

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:09.970
We don't know.

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:13.900
But there is that split second in the morning
where it just feels normal.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:16.469
I'm wondering if other people are experiencing
that.

00:06:16.469 --> 00:06:20.169
These are I think we will all remember.

00:06:20.169 --> 00:06:25.379
Living through this, those that do and of
course, tragically not everybody will, those

00:06:25.379 --> 00:08:11.740
that lived through this will certainly remember
this for the rest of our lives.

